&+WA natural &+yfiord &+Wcuts through the &+Lnarrow mountain range. &+WThe slopes
&+Ware extremely and impossible to ascend. The &+BWaters of the Abyss&+W lay
&+Wto the west. A stout &+Lstone &+Wpier hugs the inlet providing access to
&+Wnaval ships. A well made wagon trail lays to the east fashioned from
&+rred brick pavers. &+WThe &+bfiord &+Wis home to a small merchant harbor.
&+mSilks, &+yspices, &+ganimal hides, &+cmetals,&+W and &+Rrough gems &+Ware often the
&+Wmain cargo of incoming ships. There is a lot of foot traffic, since
&+Wthe approach to the fiord is extremely narrow.
