#620605
&+LThe Back of a &+rLarge &+LCavern&n~
&+L   The back of this large cavern is partially overcome by the snow and ice that
&+Lhas accumulated at these high altitudes.  The &+rBloodfist &+LMountain range
&+Lstretches off towards the north and west for quite some distance from here.  Not
&+Lfar to the north, a &+Wsnowy valley&+L can be seen.  There appears to be a crack
&+Lwithin the ground that leads downwards, quickly becoming an open ravine that
&+Lfalls away towards the valley below.&n
~
5000 134250496 25 0
D1
~
~
0 0 620606
D5
~
~
0 0 87700
S
#620606
&+LAn Entrance to a Huge &+rCavern&n~
&+L   A rather ominous and huge cavern entrance looks out upon the &+rBloodfist
&+Lmountain range here, its entrance partially obscured by ice-covered boulders.
&+LThere are traces of this cavern being used recently by a mature dragon.  Bones
&+Lof some large creature have been tossed against a wall, where the splinters
&+Lreturned to the ground and created a rather impressively spiked pile of detritus.
&+LThere is a lingering smell of dragon breath in the air as well.&n
~
